        "subject": "LU-21061 quota: add inode limits to pools with MDTs",
        "message": "LU-21061 quota: add inode limits to pools with MDTs\n\nA pool can list MDTs, but the quota master keeps only block limits\nfor pools: qmt_pool_add() rejects any member that is not an OST, and\n\"lfs setquota --pool\" refuses inode limits.\n\nKeep the inode side of a pool in an MD quota pool of the same name.\nqmt_pool_add() creates it with the first MDT of the pool and adds\nMDT members to it, and qmt_pool_del() destroys it with the pool.\nThe existing lookup by target index then applies its limits when an\nMDT of the pool acquires inode quota.  Let \"lfs setquota --pool\" set\ninode limits, also as defaults, for a pool that lists MDTs.  The\ninode limits of a pool whose last MDT is removed are kept but no\nlonger enforced.\n\nAlso take the other limit of a pool default from the pool default,\nnot from the global one, when only a hard or soft limit is given.\n\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=sanity-quota env=ONLY=\"1 92\"\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: Ife0159698ccb23a356ccbe9cd8ea2b0b2d00ef02\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
